<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN"
  "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
The PrivacyFence daemon as a LaunchDaemon, running under
its own dedicated account.

Every packaged install runs the daemon this way (ADR 0003); the per-user
LaunchAgent (com.privacyfence.app.plist in the repo root) is for a
source/dev checkout only. The
difference that matters is UserName below: a LaunchAgent runs as whoever is
logged in -- which is also who the AI agent PrivacyFence exists to govern
runs as -- and a LaunchDaemon runs as the account it names, in no login
session at all. That one line is what takes settings.yaml, the enrolled
WebAuthn credentials and the audit log's HMAC key out of the agent's reach.

Installed to /Library/LaunchDaemons/com.privacyfence.daemon.plist, root:wheel
0644, by scripts/macos_privilege_separation.sh -- which fills in every
placeholder below. Do not install this file by hand: launchd will start
the daemon happily enough, but nothing will have created the service account,
moved the data directory, or written the marker file every PrivacyFence
process reads to agree on where that directory now is
(src/privacyfence/privilege_separation.py).

The companion app -- which is what a human actually interacts with once the
daemon has no login session of its own -- is the separate LaunchAgent in
com.privacyfence.companion.plist.tmpl. ADR 0002's "startup wiring inverts on
all three platforms" is these two files, on this one.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>__DAEMON_LABEL__</string>

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>__DAEMON_EXECUTABLE__</string>
  </array>

  <!-- The whole point of this file. Both are the dedicated system account
       scripts/macos_privilege_separation.sh creates; GroupName is also the
       group the installing human is added to, which is what lets the
       companion and the daemon still reach each other's sockets under
       handoff/ while everything else stays 0700. -->
  <key>UserName</key>
  <string>__SERVICE_ACCOUNT__</string>
  <key>GroupName</key>
  <string>__SERVICE_GROUP__</string>

  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>__SYSTEM_ROOT__</string>

  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>

  <!-- Restart automatically if the daemon exits unexpectedly -- same
       contract the LaunchAgent had, and the same one the Linux systemd unit
       and the Windows Scheduled Task carry (see tests/windows_task_contract.py). -->
  <key>KeepAlive</key>
  <dict>
    <key>SuccessfulExit</key>
    <false/>
  </dict>

  <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
  <integer>5</integer>

  <!-- A daemon with no login session has no Aqua session to draw in and
       should not be scheduled as if it did. -->
  <key>ProcessType</key>
  <string>Background</string>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>__SYSTEM_ROOT__/logs/launchd.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>__SYSTEM_ROOT__/logs/launchd.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
